(6249862, 922598, 75651, '<td valign="top">You really make that tree seem almost powerless to whats about to come -OR- It stands strong amongst a passing storm.  Either way, it tells a great story.  I wish this one did better in the challenge, because I love the dynamics of it.  Very nice job!</td>', 'You really make that tree seem almost powerless to whats about to come -OR- It stands strong amongst a passing storm.  Either way, it tells a great story.  I wish this one did better in the challenge, because I love the dynamics of it.  Very nice job!', '2010-12-09 11:45:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6249976, 921850, 30861, '<td valign="top">The "bug" is a Robber Fly...<br/> <br/>As for the shot itself, I bet it would have done a lot better if you had rotated it 90 degrees clockwise. and used a gradient to darken what would become the foreground wood. I will take a stab at it...</td>', 'The "bug" is a Robber Fly... As for the shot itself, I bet it would have done a lot better if you had rotated it 90 degrees clockwise. and used a gradient to darken what would become the foreground wood. I will take a stab at it...', '2010-12-09 14:48:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6249984, 921850, 30861, '<td valign="top">Something like this might have fared better. It could have been accomplished better from the full size image of course... I did this from a screen capture of your entry.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=924454" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_924454.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_924454.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_924454.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>R.<br/></td>', 'Something like this might have fared better. It could have been accomplished better from the full size image of course... I did this from a screen capture of your entry.   R.', '2010-12-09 15:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6249990, 921850, 68504, '<td valign="top">I think Bear has it right. People seem to prefer what looks like the missionary position.</td>', 'I think Bear has it right. People seem to prefer what looks like the missionary position.', '2010-12-09 15:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6250188, 921850, 93565, '<td valign="top">I think the biggest issue here is that robber flies are an oft used subject and any shot of one that you enter is going to be compared to all the work of others, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67145" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Roz</a> being one of them. Dragonflies are the same way- <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=810742" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810742.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810742.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810742.jpg"/></a> That got a 5.77 in a FS. If you don''t elevate them to a very high level, you''ll score par at best.</td>', 'I think the biggest issue here is that robber flies are an oft used subject and any shot of one that you enter is going to be compared to all the work of others,  Roz being one of them. Dragonflies are the same way-  That got a 5.77 in a FS. If you don''t elevate them to a very high level, you''ll score par at best.', '2010-12-09 20:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6250372, 921850, 113591, '<td valign="top">I must say the wall looks quite red on my screen. The focus on the bugs are a bit soft, did you have the camera on a tripod? 1/40 sec may not be fast enough to get good handheld closeup shots. Me and my friend have started taking macro shots, and really, it is a difficult art to get the buggers nicely in focus, no matter what lens one uses. From what I''ve heard, that is the most critical aspect to get right. You should see us running around from bush to bush with a camera on it''s tripod. Hilarious. I didn''t buy a lens, bought the set of 3 Kenko tubes, they work brilliantly. I still have my arm and leg as well.</td>', 'I must say the wall looks quite red on my screen. The focus on the bugs are a bit soft, did you have the camera on a tripod? 1/40 sec may not be fast enough to get good handheld closeup shots. Me and my friend have started taking macro shots, and really, it is a difficult art to get the buggers nicely in focus, no matter what lens one uses. From what I''ve heard, that is the most critical aspect to get right. You should see us running around from bush to bush with a camera on it''s tripod. Hilarious. I didn''t buy a lens, bought the set of 3 Kenko tubes, they work brilliantly. I still have my arm and leg as well.', '2010-12-10 01:20:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6250615, 922520, 59267, '<td valign="top">Strong composition and color! its eye instantly draw my attention. Awesome shot!</td>', 'Strong composition and color! its eye instantly draw my attention. Awesome shot!', '2010-12-10 12:11:12.000000', NULL, 0),
